===Etymology 2===
{{back-form|curator}}

====Verb====

{{en-verb|curat|es}}

# {{context|transitive|lang=en}} To act as a [[curator]] for.
#: ''She '''curated''' the traveling exhibition.''
#: ''They carefully '''curated''' the recovered artifacts.''
# {{context|transitive|lang=en}} To apply selectivity and taste to, as a collection of fashion items or web pages.
#*{{quote-journal|year=2007|date=May 16|title=TV Networks Woo Advertisers with Fall Line-Up|journal=NPR_TalkNation|passage=What I love about DVRs is that they really allow you to '''curate''' your experience of television.}}
#*{{quote-journal|year=2010|date=May|volume=196|issue=2|page=151-158|title=This Land Is Our Land|author=David Biespiel|journal=Poetry|passage=During the past five years I had the good fortune to be editor of Poetry Northwest. The magazine's mission includes '''curating''' a dialogue between poetry, the other arts, and civic life.}}
#*{{quote-news|year=2010|date=November 28|section=Style|page=G1|title=Shopping sites redefine fashion|author=Laura Compton|work=San Francisco Chronicle|passage= To grasp how this all works, think of the concepts of editing and '''curating''', adopted from publishing and art but now used constantly in the fashion world to imply judgment, taste and discernment.}}
#*{{quote-journal|year=2011|date=February|volume=188|issue=2|page=105|title=Digital Clinic|author=Seth Porges|journal=Popular Mechanics|passage=From there, click the Notifications tab and scroll down to Groups. This will bring up a page that allows you to '''curate''' what sort of Group-related activity results in e-mail alerts.}}
#*{{quote-news|title=TechBits: Fab lets you shop, if not sort|work=Washington Post|date=June 10|year=2012|passage=Sometimes, you just want to shop for the pure joy of looking at cool things. And the app for Fab, a '''curated''' shopping site, is just the place to do that.}}
# {{context|intransitive|lang=en}} To work or act as a curator.
#: ''Not only does he '''curate''' for the museum, he manages the office and fund-raises.''

